Important interview concept: Best, Average and Worst Case
                                
                                 int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
                                
                                int target = 10;
                                
                                for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
                                
                                    if (arr[i] == target) {
                                        System.out.println("Found");
                                        break;
                                    }
                                }
                                
                                
                                Case	Situation	Complexity
                                Best	Element at first position	O(1)
                                Average	Element around middle	O(n)
                                Worst	Element at last position or absent	O(n)
                                
                                Interview point: Big O generally describes the upper-bound growth of an algorithm,
                                    commonly used to express worst-case complexity.
